{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Vanessa and The Rude Customer"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Keeping Your Cool"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "scholar > Food for Thought > Dividing the Chicken"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 5}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use important information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le05ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Being Persuasive"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you work in a restaurant or a shop, it is important to be persuasive to be able to change a customer's mind about something.<br><br>Remember to be polite and use appropriate expressions to persuade someone."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use expressions like <span class=\"italic\">Don't you think ... ?</span> , <span class=\"italic\">Don't you agree ... ?</span>  or <span class=\"italic\"> ... if you see what I mean</span> to convince or persuade someone to change their minds."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use modals like <span class=\"italic\">should</span>, <span class=\"italic\">ought to</span> or <span class=\"italic\">would</span> rather to suggest what is necessary."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Ann</span>: Can't the chef change my menu? <br/> <span class=\"strong\">Waiter</span>: I'm awfully sorry, but the chef is very proud of his work, <span class=\"strong\">if you see what I mean</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Example</span>: <span class=\"italic\">Don't you agree that we should leave soon?</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Here, \"Don't you agree\" politely persuades someone to leave. The use of \"should\" suggests that leaving is necessary. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Offering Advice and Solutions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you work in a restaurant or in a shop, it is important to offer advice and solutions properly.<br>Remember to offer advice politely and to use the modals <span class=\"italic\">could</span>, <span class=\"italic\">should</span> or <span class=\"italic\">might</span> to propose a solution."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Here is a list of expressions you can use to offer advice and solutions:<br>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>You might want to ... </li> <li>Would you mind ... ?</li> <li>You should</li> <li>You ought to ... </li></ul>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Ann</span>: I'm vegetarian. Do you have anything without meat? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Bob</span>: Our set lunch doesn't have anything vegetarian. You might want to try some a la carte items."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "set lunch "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a combination of courses chosen by the chef for a fixed price "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Our set lunch has a vegetarian option."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le05ob06aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear at a restaurant."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Waldorf salad "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a salad with apple, walnut and celery"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: Our Waldorf salad is excellent."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le05ob06aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "slow-cooked "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "cooked at low temperature for several hours "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You should try our slow-cooked beef shank."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le05ob06aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "guest "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a patron; customer"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: We have a wide assortment of vegetarian options for our vegetarian guests."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le05ob06aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "substitution"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "change"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: I'm sorry, but we do not offer menu substitutions for lunch."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le05ob06aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "particular "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "careful about details"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: Our chef is very particular about his creations."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le05ob06aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "susceptible "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " likely to change to another state or feeling "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Our chef is susceptible to bad moods."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le05ob06aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to wield "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to use a weapon or tool "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Vanessa wields the knife like a professional."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le05ob06aud08"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online and find information about customer service practices in 5 countries of your choice."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Is good customer service important? Is the customer always right?"}, {"type": "text"